# 7. ALLOW MULTIPLE DECLARATIONS

The Student may have more than one achievement satisfying a requirement.

Example:

**Tình nguyện tốt**

1. Tham gia Chiến dịch Mùa hè xanh.
2. Tham gia Chủ nhật xanh.
3. Tham gia hiến máu tình nguyện.

All legitimate declarations must remain visible.

Do not enforce:

"One declaration per criterion."

Do not enforce:

"One declaration per selected form."

unless the existing approved policy specifically does so.

The user may voluntarily submit additional achievements even after satisfying the minimum requirement.

Preserve multiple evidence files on each declaration.

---

# 8. ONE_OF / AT_LEAST_N / ALL_REQUIRED

The Student interface must correctly distinguish mandatory and alternative requirements.

## Mandatory

Show required requirements clearly.

## Alternatives

Let the Student choose one or more qualifying forms as permitted.

Do not automatically preselect one form just because the UI needs an initial value.

Do not mark every unselected alternative as incomplete or failed.

Do not disable adding another valid alternative after the first one has been selected.

### Example

A criterion requires at least one of two qualifying forms.

The Student declares Option A.

The UI may show Option B as:

"Phương án khác"

with a discreet Add action.

It must not force the Student to complete Option B.

### Important

The frontend should display rules and advisory completion indicators correctly.

Do not introduce hard submission blockers based solely on preliminary eligibility warnings unless an existing approved lifecycle rule explicitly requires them.

The customer previously confirmed that advisory warnings must not automatically prevent application submission.

