# 9. COMPACT DECLARATION EDITOR

Choose the interaction pattern based on actual usability.

Preferred options:

- Inline expandable form.
- Compact dialog.
- Responsive sheet for mobile where appropriate.

Do not implement multiple separate editing steps.

## Desired visual structure

Title:

"Thêm kê khai"

Context:

"Tiêu chí Tình nguyện tốt"

Input:

"Nội dung kê khai"

Evidence:

"Đính kèm minh chứng"

Primary action:

"Thêm kê khai"

Secondary:

"Hủy"

### Avoid

- Huge multi-step modal.
- Nested dialogs.
- Multiple long instructional panels.
- Redundant field-group cards.
- Separate Save Evidence and Save Declaration steps where they can be safely combined.
- English technical labels.
- Overly decorative AI-style explanatory content.

### Editing

When a Student edits an existing authorized declaration, use the same compact editor prefilled with the actual saved values.

Do not reset attachments unexpectedly.

Do not save unrelated draft fields when editing another declaration.

